<body>
<header class="decision-hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Family Travel Decision Dashboard</p>
    <h1>Epic Family Vacation: 31-Trip Comparison</h1>
    <p class="lead">A data-first ranking of 31 finished comparison itineraries (22 ranked, 9 excluded by family decision) &mdash; every score re-derived from the built-out trip pages (budget rollups, flight chains, verified June sea temps, PTO math) across ten axes. The eleven short escapes below use the same evidence standard but stay outside this two-week ranking. The numbers, at a glance:</p>
  </div>
</header>

<nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Page sections">
  <details class="site-nav-menu">
    <summary><span>Sections</span></summary>
    <div class="site-nav-links">
      <a href="locations/completed/">Completed Trips →</a>
      <a href="#trip-length">Short vs Full</a>
      <a href="#short-trips">Short Trips</a>
      <a href="#trips">Trips</a>
      <a href="locations/trip-builder/">Trip Builder →</a>
      <a href="locations/compare/">Compare by Country →</a>
      <a href="#decision">Quick Decision</a>
      <a href="#mid-trip-flights">Flight Desk</a>
      <a href="#scoreboard">Scoreboard</a>
      <a href="#length">Length Verdicts</a>
      <a href="#winners">Category Winners</a>
      <a href="#matrix">Full Matrix</a>
      <a href="#risks">Risks</a>
    </div>
  </details>
</nav>

<main>
  <section id="overview">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Plan at a Glance</p>
    <div class="overview">
      <div class="ocard"><b>31 + 11</b><span>comparison plans plus eleven short escapes (22 ranked, 9 excluded)</span></div>
      <div class="ocard"><b>{{ hub.activeTrips[0].totalBaked }}/55</b><span>top default score: {{ hub.activeTrips[0].displayName }}; booking gates still apply</span></div>
      <div class="ocard"><b>5 hybrids</b><span>Madeira/mainland &times; Crete/Sicily/Mallorca grid</span></div>
      <div class="ocard"><b data-preserve-date>June 24-26</b><span>Full days in Pittsburgh protected</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% include "hub/trip-length.njk" %}

  <section id="short-trips">
    <div class="short-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">New · 7 Nights or Less</p>
      <h2>Short, easy escapes</h2>
      <p>Smaller-budget trips built around fewer bases, lighter logistics, and enough breathing room to feel like a vacation. Warm water is a bonus here, not the price of admission.</p>
      <p class="short-method"><b>Ranked only against each other:</b> budget and ease count double; weather, fire safety, swimming, variety, food, risk, and PTO count once. Ties favor fewer PTO days, then the lower budget ceiling.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="short-grid">
      {%- for trip in shortTrips %}
      <a class="short-card" href="{{ trip.href }}">
        <div class="short-photo"><img src="{{ trip.heroImage }}" alt="{{ trip.heroAlt }}" loading="lazy"><span class="short-badge">#{{ trip.shortRank }} · {{ trip.pto.nights }} nights</span><span class="short-score">{{ trip.shortScore }}/55</span></div>
        <div class="short-body">
          <span class="short-dates">{{ trip.travelWindow[0] | displayDate }}–{{ trip.travelWindow[1] | displayDate }}</span>
          <h3>{{ trip.displayName }}</h3>
          <p>{{ trip.blurb }}</p>
          <p class="short-verdict">{{ trip.shortVerdict }}</p>
          <div class="short-stats">
            <div class="short-stat"><span>Family budget</span><b>${{ (trip.budget.floorUsd / 1000) | round(1) }}k–${{ (trip.budget.ceilUsd / 1000) | round(1) }}k</b></div>
            <div class="short-stat"><span>PTO</span><b>{{ trip.pto.days }} days</b></div>
            <div class="short-stat"><span>Home bases</span><b>{% if trip.metrics.baseMoves != null %}{{ trip.metrics.baseMoves + 1 }}{% else %}Minimal{% endif %}</b></div>
            <div class="short-stat"><span>Swimming</span><b>{% if trip.facets.swimType == 'geothermal' %}Warm geothermal{% elif trip.facets.swimType == 'warm-sea-plus-thermal' %}{{ trip.facets.swimTempF[1] }}°F sea + thermal{% elif trip.facets.heatedSwimTempF %}Pool + Atlantic{% else %}{{ trip.facets.swimTempF[0] }}–{{ trip.facets.swimTempF[1] }}°F water{% endif %}</b></div>
            <div class="short-stat"><span>Fire disruption</span><b>{{ trip.fireRisk.level }} · {{ trip.fireRisk.chanceBand }}</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="short-ready">{{ trip.readiness.label }} →</div>
        </div>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="fire-risk">
    <p class="eyebrow">New decision factor</p>
    <h2>Wildfire disruption by location and season</h2>
    <p>These bands estimate the chance that fire, smoke, evacuation, road or park closures, or related flight disruption materially changes the itinerary during its exact dates. They are conservative planning estimates inferred from official recent evidence and fire history—not promises or actuarial forecasts. Each trip takes the least-safe score among its route segments.</p>
    <div class="rubric-note"><b>Higher is safer:</b> 5 = very low (&lt;2%); 4 = low (2&ndash;5%); 3 = moderate (5&ndash;10%); 2 = high (10&ndash;20%); 1 = very high (&gt;20%). Recheck official daily danger maps and active incidents 14 days, 72 hours, and each morning before rural drives or hikes. A live red/extreme warning overrides the historical band.</div>
    <div class="matrix-wrap"><table class="budget-tbl"><thead><tr><th>Location and trip window</th><th>Planning chance</th><th>Safety score</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      {%- for id, profile in fireRisk.profiles %}
      <tr><td><b>{{ profile.name }}</b></td><td>{% if profile.score == 5 %}Very low · &lt;2%{% elif profile.score == 4 %}Low · 2&ndash;5%{% elif profile.score == 3 %}Moderate · 5&ndash;10%{% elif profile.score == 2 %}High · 10&ndash;20%{% else %}Very high · &gt;20%{% endif %}</td><td><b>{{ profile.score }}/5</b></td><td>{{ profile.rationale }}</td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section id="trips" class="shortlist">
    <div class="sl-head">
      <p class="sl-eyebrow">Trip Shortlist</p>
    <h2>Twenty-two ranked ways to spend the same two weeks</h2>
      <p>Ranked by the scoreboard — pure data, no preference thumb on the scale; the top score is outlined in red. Tap any card for the full day-by-day itinerary. Nights pill = hotel (bed) nights; the <b>+1</b> chip is the red-eye/travel night away.</p>
    </div>
    {% include "hub/cards.njk" %}
  </section>

  <section id="decision">
    <p class="eyebrow">Decision Console</p>
    <h2>Choose the priority</h2>
    <p>The default ranking uses Budget at double weight plus Weather, Fire safety, Swim, Variety, Ease, Food, Risk, Nights, and Novelty; PTO is displayed and available for custom weighting. Fire safety is the evidence-based planning chance that wildfire, smoke, evacuation, or closures materially disrupt the exact route during its exact dates. Scores remain provisional where exact 2027 schedules, complete quote sets, or next-season fire conditions are still unverified. Nine trips are excluded by family decision: <b>Albania</b>, <b>Balkans</b>, <b>California</b>, <b>Canary Islands</b>, <b>Croatia</b>, <b>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</b>, <b>Southern France</b>, <b>Spain</b>, and <b>Turkish Riviera</b>. Click a row to highlight that trip in the scoreboard.</p>
    <div class="matrix-wrap">
      <table class="decision-table"><thead><tr><th>If you're optimizing for&hellip;</th><th>Winner</th><th>Runner-up</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in hub.priorityRows %}<tr class="decision-row{% if loop.first %} on{% endif %}" data-priority="{{ row.id }}" data-trip="{{ row.winner.token }}"><td>{{ row.label }}</td><td>{{ row.winner.displayName }}</td><td>{{ row.runner.displayName }}</td><td>Preset weights from the shared engine. Default score {{ row.winner.totalBaked }}/55; default rank #{{ row.winner.appealRank }}. Net {{ row.winner.budget.floorUsd | money }}–{{ row.winner.budget.ceilUsd | money }}; gross {{ row.winner.budget.grossFloorUsd | money }}–{{ row.winner.budget.grossCeilUsd | money }}. {{ row.winner.routeReadiness }}.</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="scoreboard">
    <p class="eyebrow">Scoreboard</p>
    <h2>Fast read on the tradeoffs</h2>
    <div class="rubric-note"><b>How these scores work:</b> For the 22 ranked trips, Budget uses net cost after a single $2,000 Capital One travel credit; gross cash is also shown. Budget is weighted <b>double</b> against your $12k target / $15k strongly preferred maximum; Weather, <b>Fire safety</b>, Swim, Variety, Ease, Food, Risk, <b>Nights</b>, and <b>Novelty</b> are each rated 1-5 once. Total is out of 55 (PTO is tracked as data but not part of the default total). Fire safety is higher-is-safer: 5 = &lt;2%, 4 = 2&ndash;5%, 3 = 5&ndash;10%, 2 = 10&ndash;20%, and 1 = &gt;20% planning chance of a material wildfire disruption during the exact dates. The bands combine official recent evidence, fire history, seasonality, route exposure, and itinerary flexibility; they are not actuarial forecasts. Live warnings always override them. <b>Nights</b> rewards trip length: 12+ nights &rarr; 5, 11 &rarr; 4, 10 &rarr; 3, 9 &rarr; 2, 8 or fewer &rarr; 1. <b>Novelty</b> scores route overlap against places already visited. Card order follows this table; default ties prefer a range within the budget preference, then fewer PTO days, then lower budget ceiling and floor. Cost never removes an itinerary. Explicit family exclusions stay visible but unranked.</div>
    <div class="score-legend"><span class="good"><i></i>Green = preferred / strong</span><span class="mixed"><i></i>Amber = workable tradeoff</span><span class="weak"><i></i>Rust = weak fit</span></div>
    <div id="scenario-panel" class="scenario-panel" hidden></div>
    <div id="filter-bar" class="filter-bar" hidden></div>
    <div id="weight-panel" class="weight-panel" hidden></div>
    <div id="compare-bar" class="compare-bar" hidden></div>
    <div class="matrix-wrap"><table class="compare-table scoreboard"><thead><tr><th data-sort="trip">Trip</th><th data-sort="budget">Budget (&times;2)</th><th data-sort="weather">Weather</th><th data-sort="fireRisk">Fire safety</th><th data-sort="swim">Swim</th><th data-sort="variety">Variety</th><th data-sort="ease">Ease</th><th data-sort="food">Food</th><th data-sort="risk">Risk</th><th data-sort="nights">Nights</th><th data-sort="novelty">Novelty</th><th data-sort="pto">PTO</th><th data-sort="total">Total /55</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% include "hub/scoreboard.njk" %}
</tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section id="length">
    <p class="eyebrow">Length Verdicts</p>
    <h2>Where the days are doing real work</h2>
    <div class="budget-scroll"><table class="budget-tbl length-table"><tr><th>Trip</th><th>Length verdict</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Portugal</b></td><td>12 nights is right.</td><td>Three bases stay calm; the cold-water issue does not improve enough by cutting or stretching the route.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Madeira + Crete</b></td><td>13 hotel nights plus the outbound travel night.</td><td>Funchal 4 + Lisbon buffer 1 + Chania 6 + Rethymno 2 matches the canonical calendar. The sixth Chania night protects the hiking load; the Lisbon buffer protects the onward connection.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Madeira + Sicily</b></td><td>13 nights away / 12 hotel nights, and it is maxed out.</td><td>Five Funchal nights plus the Tuesday LIS-PMO hinge force Sicily down to six nights and two bases; there is no room left to re-add Ortigia without breaking the budget or the calendar.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Portugal + Crete</b></td><td>13 nights away / 12 hotel nights is right.</td><td>Five Portugal + seven Crete nights is the honest balance: Cascais 5, Chania 4, Rethymno 3. It keeps the signature Crete water days and one realistic gorge without reducing Portugal to a stopover.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Crete</b></td><td>13 hotel nights is right.</td><td>Chania 5 + Rethymno 3 + Agios Nikolaos 5 gives the west, south coast and Mirabello Bay distinct chapters, including one unhurried bonus day, without adding an internal flight or a fourth base.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Portugal + Sicily</b></td><td>12 hotel nights is right, but it is the busiest 12.</td><td>Five Portugal + seven Sicily nights across three bases is the max before transfer days start crowding out beach days; do not add a fourth base.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Hawaii</b></td><td>9 hotel nights plus red-eye is tight but efficient.</td><td>One more hotel night improves comfort but pushes harder against the preferred maximum.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Maui + Kauai</b></td><td>12 hotel nights is the minimum fair version.</td><td>Five Kīhei, four Poʻipū and three Princeville nights preserve a Hāna recovery day and keep western and northern Kauai drives rational; do not add a third island.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</b></td><td>12 nights is experientially right; 11 nights is the preference-fit trim.</td><td>The Sorrento/Campania leg is the budget pressure point.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Turkish Riviera</b></td><td>12 nights is right.</td><td>Antalya wants 3, Kas/Kalkan wants 4, and Fethiye/Oludeniz wants 5 to avoid rushing the best water days.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Croatia</b></td><td>12 nights is still right.</td><td>The issue is not length; it is whether repeating Croatia right after last year's trip is worth it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Southern France</b></td><td>8 nights is the correct short version.</td><td>Expanding it weakens the budget case without solving swim-water limitations.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Balkans</b></td><td>12 hotel nights is the defensible version.</td><td>The July 1-14 correction preserves the route, but price discipline now matters more than length.</td></tr>
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <section id="winners"><p class="eyebrow">Default score leaders</p><h2>What the numbers favor</h2><p>Raw rank is not booking readiness. A reroute-required concept remains visible but must be rebuilt before purchase. Net costs use $2,000 fixed travel credit; no award-seat savings are assumed.</p><div class="winner-grid">{% for t in hub.activeTrips %}{% if loop.index <= 6 %}<article class="winner-card" data-winner="{{ t.slug }}"><h3>#{{ t.appealRank }} · {{ t.displayName }}</h3><p>{{ t.totalBaked }}/55 · {{ t.budget.floorUsd | money }}–{{ t.budget.ceilUsd | money }} net</p><p>Gross {{ t.budget.grossFloorUsd | money }}–{{ t.budget.grossCeilUsd | money }} · {{ t.routeReadiness }}</p></article>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</div></section>

  <section id="matrix"><p class="eyebrow">Full Comparison</p><h2>The practical call</h2><div class="budget-scroll"><table class="budget-tbl matrix-tbl"><tr><th>Trip</th><th>Gross cash</th><th>Net after miles</th><th>Decision / booking gate</th></tr>{% for t in hub.activeTrips %}<tr data-matrix-trip="{{ t.slug }}"><td>#{{ t.appealRank }} · {{ t.displayName }}</td><td>{{ t.budget.grossFloorUsd | money }}–{{ t.budget.grossCeilUsd | money }}</td><td>{{ t.budget.floorUsd | money }}–{{ t.budget.ceilUsd | money }}</td><td>{{ t.totalBaked }}/55 · {{ t.routeReadiness }}. {{ t.cardSummary }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}<tr><th colspan="4">Excluded references — unchanged cash basis</th></tr><tr><td><b>Albania</b></td><td>Accursed Mountains hiking plus clear Riviera water at an unusually strong $9.7k&ndash;14.23k band.</td><td>Long two-stop PIT/Tirana routing and family preference override the raw score.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 39/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Southern France</b></td><td>Riviera and Provence depth with zero internal flights.</td><td>Only moderate swim fit and a premium $13.35k&ndash;19.1k band.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 39/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Italy: Salento-Amalfi</b></td><td>Food, beaches, Maratea, Capri, Amalfi/Ravello, Procida, and only three bases.</td><td>The $11.4k&ndash;16.3k band crosses preference and repeats parts of prior Italy travel.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 37/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Spain</b></td><td>The strongest Alhambra/Mezquita/Alc&aacute;zar history package with a within-preference $8.8k&ndash;14.8k band.</td><td>Heat, timed-entry pressure, nine PTO days, and family preference override the score.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 37/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Canary Islands</b></td><td>Macaronesian forest and Teide's volcanic desert on Tenerife, then La Palma's caldera.</td><td>The exact PIT&ndash;TFS route currently takes two stops, plus an inter-island flight.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 36/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Turkish Riviera</b></td><td>The warmest non-Hawaii sea on the board, plus Antalya ruins, Kalkan coves, Kekova, and &Ouml;l&uuml;deniz.</td><td>June heat, scoped advisory, long PIT logistics, and a $12.2k&ndash;18.4k band.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 36/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Croatia</b></td><td>Proven Europe logistics and warm Adriatic water.</td><td>It repeats the 2026 Split/Hvar/Korčula trip, producing a novelty score of 1/5.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 35/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Balkans</b></td><td>The most adventurous cross-border coast-and-mountain route.</td><td>July pricing, border/car rules, long drives, ferry timing, and family-friction risk.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 32/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>California Pacific Coast</b></td><td>The best mainland no-passport road trip with 12 hotel nights.</td><td>Cold water outside San Diego, a long driving load, and a $16.2k high case.</td><td><b>Excluded reference at 30/55 by family decision.</b></td></tr>
    </table></div>
    <p class="source-note">Comparison basis: 31 plans (22 ranked, 9 excluded by family decision) across an early-June-to-August planning range. Jun 6 is the nominal start, with Spain (Jun 3) and Hawaii (Jun 5) retained as explicit early-departure options. A Jun 23 return to Pittsburgh is acceptable and preferred, including an evening arrival; the only hard calendar rule is that the family must be in Pittsburgh all day Jun 24-26. Budgets are planning bands, not booking quotes, and several high cases exceed the $15k preferred maximum. Exact-date flight inventory was refreshed Sep 10, 2026; component fares are volatile snapshots, not held tickets, and every critical chain still needs a complete family checkout with seats, bags, and ticket protection.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="risks"><p class="eyebrow">Booking gates</p><h2>What the scores cannot promise</h2><ul class="hc-list"><li>Only the 22 ranked comparison trips received this points-adjusted audit. The nine excluded references and separate short-escape band retain their original basis.</li><li>No four-seat award itinerary is confirmed. The rankable credit is $2,000, not a transfer valuation.</li><li>Gross cash remains visible. Lodging, car coverage, food and activities are planning allowances; no inventory is held.</li><li>Iceland + Ischia/Cilento remains reroute-required. Its score does not make its old airfare construction bookable.</li><li>Keep Pittsburgh June 24–26 entirely clear. Reject late returns and unprotected connections even if a fare looks cheaper.</li></ul></section>

  <section id="considered">
    <p class="eyebrow">Options Considered</p>
    <h2>The "Madeira-variety" exploration &mdash; combos we weighed</h2>
    <details class="considered-box">
      <summary>Every epic-hiking / swim-variety combo we discussed, and why most weren't built</summary>
      <p class="considered-intro">Sparked by Madeira's mid-trip flight friction plus wanting a leg with epic hiking and dramatically different scenery <em>and</em> good swimming &mdash; while staying novel against the Mediterranean-beach board and our recent Mexico trip. Captured here so we don't lose the thread.</p>

      <h3 class="considered-h">Built / in progress</h3>
      <ul class="considered-list">
        <li><strong>Canary Islands</strong> (Tenerife + La Palma) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, excluded reference (36/55)</span> Madeira's ecological twin (Macaronesian laurel forest + Teide volcano) &mdash; but flight connectivity is the tradeoff, not the upgrade.</li>
        <li><strong>Albania</strong> (Accursed Mountains: Theth/Valbona + the Riviera: Ksamil) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, 39/55, excluded by family decision</span> The best <em>warm-sea + novel</em> pick: alpine drama + Caribbean-clear swimming, cheap, one-country ground transport, no island-hop trap.</li>
        <li><strong>Crete</strong> (Chania + Rethymno + Agios Nikolaos) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, #13 (37/55)</span> The standalone island route carries the full mountain-vs-sea variety: lagoons, Imbros, Preveli, Knossos, Spinalonga and Mirabello Bay with no internal flight, plus the preferred June 23 return.</li>
        <li><strong>Madeira + Mallorca</strong> &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, #4 (41/55)</span> The Madeira ridge-hiking week paired with a sandy Mediterranean swim in Mallorca. It remains the strongest Madeira hybrid, though its refreshed high case now reaches $15.9k.</li>
        <li><strong>Dolomites + Venice + Sardinia</strong> &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, #14 (37/55)</span> Best pure epic-hiking (Tre Cime, Seceda) with a Venice opener and an epic-beach Sardinia finale. Landlocked hiking half = the variety.</li>
        <li><strong>Iceland</strong> (Reykjavík + Golden Circle + South Coast + Jökuls&aacute;rl&oacute;n) &mdash; <span class="st st-go">built, #3 (42/55)</span> The most novel-looking option &mdash; nothing like the Med board or Mexico. Swim = warm geothermal lagoons, not the (cold) sea.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="considered-h">Considered, set aside</h3>
      <ul class="considered-list">
        <li><strong>Costa Rica</strong> (Arenal + Monteverde + Manuel Antonio) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">off the table</span> A complete plan already existed, but it photographs like Yucat&aacute;n/Riviera Maya &mdash; no novelty right after a Mexico trip. The look is structural (beach + jungle), so a rebuild wouldn't fix it.</li>
        <li><strong>Slovenia</strong> (Julian Alps + So&ccaron;a + Bled) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">not built</span> Genuinely novel emerald-alpine look and cheap, but the swim is turquoise river/glacial lakes, not warm sea.</li>
        <li><strong>Swiss Bernese Oberland</strong> (Lauterbrunnen + glacial lakes) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">not built</span> Epic and unique, but pushes hard past the $15k preferred maximum &mdash; the likely budget-breaker.</li>
        <li><strong>Greek mainland</strong> (Zagori/Vikos + Pelion) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">not built</span> Deepest-gorge + stone-village hiking is novel, but it's still Greece (we have Crete) and the Aegean beaches read Med.</li>
        <li><strong>Montenegro</strong> (Durmitor + Bay of Kotor) &mdash; <span class="st st-no">not built</span> Epic canyon + warm sea, but likely overlaps the existing Balkans road-trip and the coast looks Med.</li>
        <li><strong>Azores</strong> &mdash; <span class="st st-no">rejected</span> Same via-Lisbon Atlantic bottleneck as Madeira &mdash; doesn't fix the connectivity problem that started all this.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="considered-note">Also noted along the way: <strong>Corsica</strong> (already on the board inside Sardinia + Corsica) and <strong>Crete</strong> are the closest "Madeira mountain-vs-sea substitute you may already own." The recurring tension: Albania took the best warm-sea-and-novel slot, so what's left trades warm ocean (Iceland/Slovenia/Switzerland = lagoon/river/lake swim) or partly echoes the Med board (Greece/Montenegro).</p>
    </details>
  </section>

